     About 95.7% of all eligible shares participated in Berkshire's=20
1994 shareholder-designated contributions program.  Contributions=20
made through the program were $10.4 million and 3,300 charities=20
were recipients.

      Every year a few shareholders miss participating in the=20
program because they either do not have their shares registered in=20
their own names on the prescribed record date or because they fail=20
to get the designation form back to us within the 60-day period=20
allowed for its return.  Since we don't make exceptions when=20
requirements aren't met, we urge that both new shareholders and old=20
read the description of our shareholder-designated contributions=20
program that appears on pages 50-51.

     <i>To participate in future programs, you must make sure your=20
shares are registered in the name of the actual owner, not in the=20
nominee name of a broker, bank or depository.  Shares not so=20
registered on August 31, 1995 will be ineligible for the 1995=20
